  "ext.guide_html": "<h2>Extensions guide (sub-plugins)</h2>\n<p>An <b>extension</b> is a sub-plugin that adds new features to the IDE without modifying its code: once loaded, it appears as a menu entry in the <b>Extensions</b> menu.</p>\n\n<h3>1. Creating an extension</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Open <b>Extensions → Create extension (sub-plugin)…</b> and enter a name.</li>\n<li>The wizard generates <code>extension.py</code> automatically and opens it in a new IDE tab.</li>\n<li>Edit the file, adding your features.</li>\n<li>Reload with <b>Extensions → Reload extensions</b>: the new menu entry appears immediately, without restarting QGIS.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>2. Where it is saved</h3>\n<pre>qgis_python_ide/\n└── extensions/\n    └── my_extension/\n        └── extension.py</pre>\n<p>The folder name comes from the chosen name (lowercase, spaces → underscores). The file must be named exactly <code>extension.py</code>.</p>\n\n<h3>3. How loading works</h3>\n<p>At startup and on every reload the IDE scans the <code>extensions/</code> folder. Each module must expose:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>create_extension()</code> → returns an object with <code>name</code> (display name) and <code>actions</code> (list of <code>QAction</code>);</li>\n<li><code>register(window)</code> (optional) → called with the main window: create actions, docks and menus here.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>From <code>window</code> you can access: <code>window.iface</code> (QGIS interface), <code>window.tabs</code> (open editors), <code>window.i18n</code> (current language), <code>window.log</code> (log panel), <code>window.run_script()</code> (run code).</p>\n\n<h3>4. How to run it</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>After reloading, the menu entry appears under <b>Extensions</b>.</li>\n<li>Clicking the action runs the function connected via <code>action.triggered.connect(...)</code>.</li>\n<li>To call it from code: <code>window.extensions.get(\"my_extension\").run()</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>5. Minimal example</h3>\n<pre>from qgis.PyQt.QtGui import QAction\n\n\nclass MyExtension:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.name = \"My extension\"\n        self.actions = []\n\n    def register(self, window):\n        action = QAction(\"Run\", window)\n        action.triggered.connect(\n            lambda: window.iface.messageBar().pushInfo(\n                \"My extension\", \"OK\"\n            )\n        )\n        self.actions.append(action)\n\n\ndef create_extension():\n    return MyExtension()</pre>\n\n<h3>6. Rules and common issues</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Import only from <code>qgis.PyQt</code> and use fully-qualified enums (Qt6/QGIS 4 compatibility).</li>\n<li>If the extension does not appear: check the Log panel — the load error is reported with the extension name.</li>\n<li>Duplicate names: the wizard refuses to create an existing folder.</li>\n<li>To disable an extension without deleting it, rename its folder and reload.</li>\n</ul>",
